# orig-boot — run the ORIGINAL firmware binary unmodified (canonical run).
#
# Sessions 46-47 state:
#   * NO reset patch needed (session 38/41 retraction stands; the boot chain
#     is intact) — the vendor bytes execute as-is via LoadBinary @0x08004000.
#   * Harness workaround 1 (session 45): SYST_CVR=0 written at t=10 ms —
#     Renode's descending SysTick LimitTimer with CURRENT=0 first fires at
#     0xFFFFFF/fclk; silicon wraps in ~1 tick. Restate in equivalence reports.
#   * Harness workaround 2 (session 47): r9 := 0x08040000 at the init-walker
#     entry — the armlink compressed-RW-data loader adds r9 (the scatter
#     base) to RAM-base-relative table pointers; Renode's reset leaves r9=0,
#     so every table pointer lost its 0x0804 prefix and the boot's
#     table-driven init executed through broken pointers. With r9 set, the
#     firmware's own fixup code produces correct tables (0x20000000 =
#     0x08043B20).
#   * KNOWN REMAINING STALL (session 47): the prio-3 task's software-I²C
#     EEPROM master (DATA=PB9, CLK=PA11) waits for a per-byte ACK that no
#     slave model gives; the next harness item is a Python I²C-slave
#     peripheral (see session-47 log entry for the full protocol decode).
#
# The original's OSCtxSwCtr = RAM 0x200050EC, OSTime = 0x2000511C (literal
# pools 0x08027B34/0x08027B44 read out of OSIntExit/OSTimeTick).

using sysbus
mach create "hguv98-orig"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @/home/sslayer/Proyectos/HG-UV98/reconstruction/sim/gd32f103.repl

# bootloader-equivalent handoff from the ORIGINAL's own vector table
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00000000 0x20006780
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x00000004 0x08044691

sysbus Tag <0x40021004, 0x40021007> "RCC_CFGR" 0x00000008

sysbus LoadBinary @/home/sslayer/Proyectos/HG-UV98/firmware/MAIN-MCU-HG-UV98-V1.0.1-190416.bin 0x08004000

# the armlink scatter base (session 47)
cpu AddHook 0x08042900 "from Antmicro.Renode.Peripherals.CPU import RegisterValue; self.SetRegister(9, RegisterValue.Create(0x08040000, 32))"

# protocol UART output (USART2 = the 8051 link) to the console
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart2

echo "=== boot 10 ms (decompressor + SystemInit + main + OSStart) ==="
emulation RunFor "00:00:00.010"

sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0xE000E018 0x00000000

echo "=== run 100 ms — OS tick ==="
emulation RunFor "00:00:00.100"
echo "=== OSCtxSwCtr (0x200050EC):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x200050EC
echo "=== OSTime (0x2000511C):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000511C

echo "=== run 900 ms more ==="
emulation RunFor "00:00:00.900"
echo "=== OSCtxSwCtr:"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x200050EC
echo "=== OSTime:"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000511C
echo "=== fault registers (must stay 0):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0xE000ED28
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0xE000ED2C
quit
